---
import PrepLayout from '../../layouts/PrepLayout.astro';
import { PRACTICE_MODES } from '../../data/prepCurriculum';
import { SITE } from '../../consts';
if (!SITE.features.prepTools) return Astro.redirect('/questions/', 302);
---

<PrepLayout
  title="Round-specific ML interview practice method"
  description="Closed-book practice protocols, rubrics, feedback, and graduation rules for senior ML interview rounds."
  heading="Practice the round you will actually face."
  lede="An eight-minute verbal answer, a forty-minute design, and a coding implementation are different performances. Question pages now choose a timer and rubric based on the round rather than applying one generic scorecard."
>
  <p class="intro">Use Practice Mode on any <a href="/questions/">question page</a>. Scratchpad text stays in memory. If enabled by you, the local queue stores only question ID, round mode, score, weak rubric dimensions, attempt count, and due date.</p>

  <h2>Round modes</h2>
  <div class="mode-grid">
    {Object.values(PRACTICE_MODES).map((mode) => <article><header><h3>{mode.label}</h3><span>{mode.minutes} min</span></header><p>{mode.instruction}</p><ul>{mode.rubric.map((item) => <li>{item.label}</li>)}</ul></article>)}
  </div>

  <h2>The attempt–diagnose–repair loop</h2>
  <ol class="step-list">
    <li><strong>Attempt closed-book.</strong> Use the round timer and speak, derive, design, or code as the real format requires.</li>
    <li><strong>Mark observable weak dimensions.</strong> “Felt bad” is not a diagnosis; “never defined the ship decision” is.</li>
    <li><strong>Select overall evidence.</strong> Weak is due in two days; Review in one week; Confident counts toward—but does not complete—graduation.</li>
    <li><strong>Read only to repair.</strong> Compare with the reference after scoring. Write the missing mechanism, decision, test, or story evidence.</li>
    <li><strong>Retry after spacing.</strong> Use a changed follow-up or prompt. Immediate fluency after reading is not retained evidence.</li>
    <li><strong>Interleave later.</strong> Verify the repair when the category is no longer predictable.</li>
  </ol>

  <section class="callout"><h2>Graduation rule</h2><p>For a critical question or pattern, require two successful closed-book attempts on different days, no critical rubric dimension marked weak, one unfamiliar follow-up, and survival in a later mixed session.</p></section>

  <h2>How to record yourself</h2>
  <ol class="step-list">
    <li>Record audio or screen locally; do not upload confidential project detail.</li>
    <li>Watch once for content: correctness, decisions, evidence, and omissions.</li>
    <li>Watch again for delivery: answer fit, structure, hedging, silence, and response to pushback.</li>
    <li>Write one corrective behavior. Do not produce a transcript of every imperfection.</li>
    <li>For L5/L6, ask a peer to challenge at least two assumptions rather than simply listen.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>A standard 60-minute short-answer block</h2>
  <div class="time-block"><span>08 min</span><p>Closed-book answer</p><span>07 min</span><p>Rubric diagnosis</p><span>20 min</span><p>Targeted repair</p><span>08 min</span><p>Rewrite outline from memory</p><span>12 min</span><p>One changed follow-up</p><span>05 min</span><p>Schedule retry</p></div>

  <section class="callout"><h2>Self-score limitation</h2><p>A local score cannot calibrate L6 scope, story ownership, coding correctness, or room presence by itself. Use at least one <a href="/prep/simulations/">observed simulation</a> and instruct the observer to push back.</p></section>

  <p><a href="/questions/">Choose a question →</a> · <a href="/prep/progress/">Open the retry queue →</a></p>
</PrepLayout>

<style>
  .mode-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: .7rem; }
  .mode-grid article { padding: .9rem; border: 1px solid var(--c-rule); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--c-surface); }
  .mode-grid header { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: .7rem; }
  .mode-grid h3 { margin: 0 !important; }
  .mode-grid header span { flex: 0 0 auto; color: var(--c-accent); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .72rem; }
  .mode-grid p, .mode-grid li { font-size: .82rem; }
  .mode-grid ul { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .35rem; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .mode-grid li { padding: .2rem .4rem; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--c-bg-tint); }
  .time-block { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 4rem 1fr; gap: .3rem .8rem; padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--c-rule); border-radius: var(--radius); }
  .time-block span { color: var(--c-accent); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .78rem; }
  .time-block p { margin: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { .mode-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
